{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev","id":1340676,"title":"M20 v MRev","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-10T13:56:35-07:00","id":1340676,"title":"M20 v MRev","content":"So, I have always played the revised edition of WoD. When V20 came out I didn't pick it up because I had all the revised books and was told that it was the same game. so I didn't really find it was a value to me. Recently I have found myself in a Mage game and was told be various players that M20 was the best so I picked it up. As I read it though I find myself growing more frustrated with the book. <br /> <br /> My question is is it really worth switching over from Revised and why?<br /> <br /> Just to let people know, I do not find having all the rules in 1 book appealing becuase it suffers from bloat and is more difficult for me to navigate because of it, so that is not a reason to switch over in my mind. I have already had ot switch out much of the book marking to make it more manageable to search and don't even get me started on the terrors of Ctl + F for this edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T23:03:49-07:00","id":1340739,"title":"","content":"I very very much prefer M20, myself.<br /> <br /> First off, while the corebook is a tome, not all the rules and things got squeezed into it - essentially the original content planned for it instead became four books.<br /> <br /> * <b>M20 Corebook</b><br /> * <b>M20 How Do You DO That?</b> - A book that tries to give a lot of examples and explanations on how to do certain Magickal effects. Contains neat things, but also contains controversial ideas that cause some Sphere bloat. I still recommend it, if you simply treat it as &quot;The Book of Phil's Houserules&quot; and pick what you like, drop what you don't. The book itself suggests that very way of handling it.<br /> * <b>M20 Book Of Secrets</b> - More general stuff that didn't fit into core. You get almost all Merits/Flaws of all the old mage books combined, some adjusted, some neat new ones. Also more paradigms, practices, archetypes, instruments, combat maneuvers, detailed Wonder creation, rules for Child Mages, details about the justice systems among the different factions, and a big M20 FAQ<br /> * <b>M20 Gods &amp; Monsters</b> - Big book of NPC (and weird player) templates and rules (From mundane humans to gods) including a character creation system for all of that, akin to the old Bygone Bestiary book.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd get all of those; Each brings good stuff to the table, and make for a rather complete package. All you really need some of the old books for is fluff, like the Trad/Conventionbooks.<br /> <br /> Now some explanations regarding M20: The whole edition is geared towards players of pretty much all previous Editions, especially Metaplot options.<br /> <br /> * The Traditions, Technocracy and Disparate Crafts are all contained in core, and each is an equally valid group for player characters.<br /> <br /> * Metaplot events (Avatar Storm, fall of Doissetep, corruption of the Technocracy, withering of Magick, Fall of Horizon, betrayal by the Hollow Ones etc.) are all pick-your-poison-if-they-happened, in a sandbox fashion. Each &quot;Future Fates&quot; entry has explanations and points as to what choices will affect your game in what ways, and what mood they set.<br /> <br /> * Magick rules have gone back to 2nd / Sorceror's Crusade by default; The total amount of Arete successes counts for all the effect's properties (Only when using Damage + Duration at once does one of them have to be split out.). This has the advantage that you don't need a lot of extended rolls or big rituals on average to pull off things due to the small Arete dice pool, like Revised tended to demand. But the book of course also offers the optional rule of splitting up the dice for every aspect of an effect, like in Revised.<br /> <br /> * Instruments (called Foci before) are no longer bound strictly to whole spheres. Instead Mages simply use instruments in a fashion where it makes sense for their practice and effect in question - heck, they can use different instruments for the same effect, if it makes sense. Dropping instruments (i.e. foci in Rev) then allows you to do those *effects* you used to do with them without the use of an instrument. This system to me makes a lot more sense, because the Focus assignment per sphere always seemed nonsensical, given how different the effects per sphere can be, and thus called for different ways of creating them.<br /> <br /> * The Corebook has a supergood listing of how a Mage's Belief/Paradigm -&gt; Instruments (prev. called Foci) -&gt; Practice work (Now called a Mage's Focus as the total package), and Book of Secrets just expands on that. It is really really good for introducing new players to how Mages think and work, and also gives you a lot of freedom in coming up with stuff for a character.<br /> <br /> * Each Tradition/Sect/faction now has multiple affinity spheres, with the character picking one of them at chargen. Finally.<br /> <br /> * Paradox is lessened back to 2nd ed levels (Example: 1 paradox for successful vulgar effects), which means your Mages won't be constrantly buried in it for small things. Again the book offers an optional rule for &quot;Reckoning&quot; Metaplot use a la Revised and lists the old rules<br /> <br /> * As written above, the Avatar Storm is optional<br /> <br /> * Sphere Specialties!<br /> <br /> * Really good Sphere charts for common Magical effects<br /> <br /> * The Arch Sphere system(s) of the old books are *very* optional - M20 stresses that you can pretty much pull off anything with the 1-5 Sphere levels, if you are creative enough and get enough successes to do it.<br /> <br /> * Two indexes in the back! A general and a rules index. Amazing thing, given they seriously let you find the anything in those tomes.<br /> <br /> I can't list everything, really, There are a <i>lot</i> of little neat rules, adjustments, ideas, fluff and explanations, but those are the big mechanics that pop up in my head immediately. There is a lot more stuff around it all.<br /> Hope that helps!<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> It also contains a section involving the whole Hypothetical-Average-Bystander / Hypothetical-Omniscient-Observer / Rresult-based / Process-based debates among mage fans when it comes to how Magick works, what the advantages and disadvantages of each approach are, and what Mage 20 assumes by default. ( Hint, it's Hypothetical-Average-Bystander and Process-Based )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-11-2019, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T23:30:16-07:00","id":1340742,"title":"","content":"I second Ambrosia's statements. <br /> <br /> Honestly, since M20 and its accompanying books have been released I hardly ever even open my older books. When I do its usually for rather obscure tidbits. <br /> <br /> The info in M20 is simply complete enough for most of my ST needs and aside from a few fuzzy issues (Wonders) the rules and options are pretty consistent. <br /> <br /> As is often mentioned HDYDT is really the only book with questionable ideas with its sphere bloat in the mater of psychic, spiritual, and Chi effects. But even they are at least consistent in relation to themselves that if it's what you are interested in for the sake of flavor the (house)rules will work well (though my group ignores them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  Spelling 10-11-2019, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T00:01:17-07:00","id":1340746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340742#post1340742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, since M20 and its accompanying books have been released I hardly ever even open my older books. When I do its usually for rather obscure tidbits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess the other set of books that I'd still recommend for fluff aside of the Trad/Conventionbooks are location books. Book Of Worlds/Infinite Tapestry/Book Of Chantries/Horizon for all the Umbral fluff and things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-11-2019, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T00:18:01-07:00","id":1340747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340739#post1340739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sphere Specialties!</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor nitpick: These are in Revised, however the 20th books boosted the impact of Specialties, so these are even more useful than before.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> In general, I definitely agree that M20 is the best edition so far, and Ambrosia explained it well.<br /> <br /> I will, however, note one big negative to me: M20, esp. compared to the other 20th books, really bloated the size of the Ability lists, this is one of the few places where former optional rules becoming default rules was a bad thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T00:29:15-07:00","id":1340748,"title":"","content":"They really are some great books. I suggest you start with the M20 core and Book of Secrets. They are very well written and much more consistent than the old books. There still is a lot of fluff, but it is far less distracting and doesn't fog up the rules. What I love is that it is written by a gamer for gamers. Satyros doesn't pull any punches either. Another thing I love is how all the extended bits &amp; pieces are now consistent with one another. A big deal is to have <i>all</i> the Merits and Flaws assembled in one book, knowing that a singe author has read them all and made revisions as needed to preserve consistency.<br /> <br /> Now that I have typed that word, I now realize it is the beauty M20's. Consistency. Sure, you can find everything you want in all the old books, but there are innumerable minor contradictions you have to resolve. Plus there is a general sense of &quot;refinement&quot;. We have had decades of &quot;play-testing&quot; and years of feedback that guided Brutaco as he wrote the thing. And he gets personal with the reader. No hidden mysterious powers that be. He discusses various approaches, mentions the controversial rule some people might still like and puts it in there as an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T03:26:17-07:00","id":1340752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340747#post1340747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will, however, note one big negative to me: M20, esp. compared to the other 20th books, really bloated the size of the Ability lists, this is one of the few places where former optional rules becoming default rules was a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.I never really liked Secondary Abilites and such (Most seem to be covered by the primary ones) - but recently I learned that many online games treat Secondaries as giving a -1 diff when used. Some say it's in some rulebooks. I can't for the life of me find it, but it indeed immediately gives them more purpose. Else I really hardly can see any reason for most of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T05:46:18-07:00","id":1340766,"title":"","content":"I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> on this M20 vs MRev thing.<br /> <br /> A few more stuff M20 has that I think it's worth mentioning:<br /> <br /> Reality Zones:<br /> This is something I always wanted Mage to have, the Idea that the Consensus holds different power in different parts of the world (depending on the local beliefs) was always kinda floating there in the material, but this was never properly ruled. Now it is. What is Vulgar and what is Coincidental can change to some extent depending on the local consensus. This provides a more sensible background for the Ascencion War: Now to try to change the local beliefs (or protect them) makes a difference, you can trully &quot;win territory&quot; for your Paradigm (or lose it).<br /> <br /> Hazard rules and rules to break stuff. These rules help to expand and flesh out combat, and make attacking objects less polemical than before.<br /> <br /> It also has a lot of good ideas. Like other kinds of mage contests other than Certamen<br /> <br /> The only thing I really rescue from Revised it's the description of the Spheres. I find Revised chapter about Spheres to be more comprehensive. Not so much for the Rote samples as for the description that delves more on the methaphisics of each level (or at least that's the impression I get). I would recomend to read both to get ideas about what each level can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T08:43:18-07:00","id":1340782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340752#post1340752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.I never really liked Secondary Abilites and such (Most seem to be covered by the primary ones) - but recently I learned that many online games treat Secondaries as giving a -1 diff when used. Some say it's in some rulebooks. I can't for the life of me find it, but it indeed immediately gives them more purpose. Else I really hardly can see any reason for most of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the reason why some of them exist, but they are VERY situational and character-dependent. Not everyone is going to want to invest points into Archery or Flying, since not everyone needs them. Just having them isn't bad, but it might have been more helpful to put the Secondary Abilities in the Book of Secrets.<br /> <br /> Also, Flying and Jetpack really should have been shuffled into the same ability, since the differences between them are largely cosmetic. Most characters would only use one or the other anyway, so why not? Call it &quot;Flying/Jetpack&quot;, and save some space in the already massive document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T10:18:21-07:00","id":1340797,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your comments, I was hitting walls reading the books and yes I already bought them all because even if I don't use them I like ot support the company and help keep them alive and will continue to do so. <br /> <br /> The walls I kept hitting that kept anoying me were:<br /> 1. Trying ot search the book was very problematic the book marks really suck and I had to re-name them to things that made since to try and find anything quickly and Ctrl F is atrocious. the indexs are bloated and finding things in general ahs been a point of contention for me. Especially since the things we look up are things that are easily found in Revised Core rules book.<br /> 2. Every time they say &quot;this is the way we did it in Revised&quot; I just wanted to scream &quot;I don't care how old systems did it, I want to know how this edition does it, thats why I bought a new edition.&quot; it felt like they wer adding to my first problem when talking about older editions as they are adding hte same terms in that i needed to search which added to search results. Also it breaks up the flow of learning the game when I constantly have to hear, &quot;back in the old days....&quot;<br /> 3. It just felt like they put in more words to just put in more swords rather than make them worth while, too many examples yes it is nice to be clear but If i hear one more time about jennys sneaking or the hoop dance I literally am going to scream please just get to the point, and then there are tables for simple concepts that I don't know why we needed a table for that. Seriously you couldn't understand trying again without a table, really?<br /> 4. As we continued to play the game I kept hitting WTF moments with the rules like Rotes; Really they are just for story? Serriously? Then why did we even mention them let alone bloat the book talking about them at all?<br /> 5. My group literally doesn't use all the rules because &quot;The book is too big for us to know them all and looking them up at the table is not possible&quot;, so they wing it 80% of the time. We are trying ot follow the rules more but the book's size has become and obsticle to many of them wanting to learn them. Last session one of the players bought the printed book and crush our table with it. We didn't open it once during hte session to try to look up a rule but everyone felt it trying to intemidate us while we played so we put it in a corner until it can learn to play nice.<br /> <br /> So with all these things I was at my wits end with whether I should continue reading or just fall back on my knowledge of revised and say that is good enough. I know the above is not fair to the writer that put in their hard time to putting together this encyclopedia but I didn't know if it was for me or not or if I was just edition waring a bit because I am so used to Revised that I don't see why I should change to Revised+.<br /> <br /> Now that you all have pointed out some stuff that has improved, I am going to continue. I did enjoy the Magic focus stuff during character creation a lot. Not sure if I will use this with my game or not but I will at least read it and continue to play in the M20 game I am in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T13:25:26-07:00","id":1340831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340752#post1340752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.I never really liked Secondary Abilites and such (Most seem to be covered by the primary ones) - but recently I learned that many online games treat Secondaries as giving a -1 diff when used. Some say it's in some rulebooks. I can't for the life of me find it, but it indeed immediately gives them more purpose. Else I really hardly can see any reason for most of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf Revised Players Handbook, p 177.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11720_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11720\" data-vbnamecard=\"11720\">Redwulfe</a> I have a few things to respond to your post, but it's a bit long and will have to wait until later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T13:37:13-07:00","id":1340832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340831#post1340831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf Revised Players Handbook, p 177.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11720_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11720\" data-vbnamecard=\"11720\">Redwulfe</a> I have a few things to respond to your post, but it's a bit long and will have to wait until later</div> </div> </div> </div>All good, like I said I am probably just being unfair, but those were my initial feelings on the book, not having read the full thing like I should.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T16:13:52-07:00","id":1340860,"title":"","content":"M20 has a system for Resonance that I personally prefer over what MRev provided. It also revised the Quiet rules, though that's mainly a change in terminology (Jhor is now called Morbidity so that the term Jhor can go back to its original meaning of a type of Resonance; and Clarity is now called Denial, which fits it better). That said, Book of Secrets introduces the Negative Men, a variant on the Marauders who are in the thrall of Denial rather than Madness and tend to instinctively generate countermagick instead of shoving Paradox onto others. <br /> <br /> The single biggest change in the game systems is the way paradigm is handled. In particular, magical styles are no longer hardwired to your faction: that is, you don't need to be a Verbena to be a witch, or an Etherite to be a mad scientist, etc. (The opposite still holds: while not all witches are Verbena, all Verbena are witches.) It does this by splitting the Theory and Practice sections that were in the MRev Tradition write-ups into their own section of the book, independent of any faction, and having the M20 faction write-ups merely reference which ones mages in that faction subscribe to. In fact, even the list of suitable magical tools has been shifted out of the Tradition write-ups and into the Practice write-ups. <br /> <br /> (There's also a massive shift in terminology in this regard: what earlier editions called foci, M20 calls instruments; what earlier editions called Paradigm, M20 calls Focus; and what earlier editions called Theory, M20 calls Paradigm. Practice is still Practice.)<br /> <br /> One effect of these shifts is that Orphans are no longer anything-goes mages with patchwork paradigms; instead, they're \u201cmerely\u201d mages who have refused to join any of the factions. Taken as a whole, their magic is still all over the place; but considered individually, there's often little difference between an Orphan and a Traditionist other than political alignment. In MRev, if you wanted to play a witch, you'd play a Verbena; in M20, if you want to play a witch, you play a mage who Practices Witchcraft, who may or may not be a Verbena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-24-2019, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T16:33:24-07:00","id":1340864,"title":"","content":"The shift for the way paradigm is handled does look really good to me and I can hardley wait ot get to that part of the book. I am not sure on the terminology shift though as it is confusing to me. Though using Madness, Denial, and Morbidity for the various aspects of Quite is good for me and so is calling Foci Instruments. I never like using Foci in mage unless you are actually refering to Spirits bound into items. The other terminalogy shifts could have probably not happened and I would have been fine. Not sure it was neccessary and may have added to confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T18:17:33-07:00","id":1340878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340864#post1340864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I never like using Foci in mage unless you are actually refering to Spirits bound into items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to Fetishes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T19:56:35-07:00","id":1340891,"title":"","content":":eye_roll: yep, well that is great now I am getting confused on the system that I am looking at. I have been reading a lot of Shadowrun of late. So now that I am a bit on track I don\u2019t have a problem with the terminology of I either. <br /> <br /> That does bring me to the question then, Why all the terminology changes then? I can understand Clarity/Denial but the rest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T22:06:47-07:00","id":1340905,"title":"","content":"To me, the terminology just makes more sense this way. Keep in mind, up until this Summer, I had not played Mage in many many years. The line was ending just as Ars Magica 5 was taking off (though I started with ArM4, <i>after</i> playing Mage), and I went hard core with that for a ong time. Even managed to participate in writing a few books. I joined a local game group that is playing mixed WoD (retro), and jumped into Sorcerers Crusade. For the first time ever. Great game. Managed to find all the books used in great condition online for less than sixty bucks. So when I relearned the system and terminology, I started fresh from there. Wording is different (style and tools), but the shape is the same. Point being that, when I started reading about M20 and Focus, it made a lot more sense to me and it hooked me in. So I went and got a copy and some other stuff and I am quite pleased. So I didn't have to unlearn or change anything. I just had to relearn in a different way.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Ars Magica, I noticed it gets mentioned in M20 books much more than it did in old Mage books. Interestingly, they are metagame references discussing play style or historic notes. The irony is that, as far as I can tell, the actual game itself seems to be trying to disentangle itself from Ars. Except for the Order of Hermes and some House names, but even then it is a bit light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T00:04:48-07:00","id":1340916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340797#post1340797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Every time they say &quot;this is the way we did it in Revised&quot; I just wanted to scream &quot;I don't care how old systems did it, I want to know how this edition does it, thats why I bought a new edition.&quot; it felt like they wer adding to my first problem when talking about older editions as they are adding hte same terms in that i needed to search which added to search results. Also it breaks up the flow of learning the game when I constantly have to hear, &quot;back in the old days....&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering that the 20th lines were not originally envisions at a true new edition. They're anniversary editions. The idea was to create omnibus love letters to fans of the games, with some minor tweaks to address some long standing issues. Mage in particular had a large edition war between 2e and Revised, and M20 had to do a lot of work to appeal to fans of both eras of the game. So there's a seriously balancing act between the goal of being an anniversary edition, getting fixes in the game, and trying to keep things relatively accessible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. As we continued to play the game I kept hitting WTF moments with the rules like Rotes; Really they are just for story? Serriously? Then why did we even mention them let alone bloat the book talking about them at all? </div> </div> </div>Rotes has always been part of the game, and have always had this problem. This relates back to my point about what the primary goal of the book is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....because I am so used to Revised that I don't see why I should change to Revised+. </div> </div> </div>I think you might be letting the size of the text overwhelm you a bit here. While M20 has more elements of 2e in it than V20 or W20 which are mechanically much more Revised as a base, the rules haven't really changed that much. If you know the Revised rules it's a bit more of a change than if you're more used to the 2e rules (esp. regarding magic), but it's huge difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T08:01:23-07:00","id":1341093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340782#post1340782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the reason why some of them exist, but they are VERY situational and character-dependent. Not everyone is going to want to invest points into Archery or Flying, since not everyone needs them. Just having them isn't bad, but it might have been more helpful to put the Secondary Abilities in the Book of Secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have long disliked &quot;skill creep&quot;, as the end result is that you have to spread the same number of building points thinner and thinner, leaving starting characters less competent. GURPS was especially bad about it. I found that when I whittled WoD down to just 24 fairly broad abilities (8 each of talents, skills, and knowlege) and adopted Exalted's speciality system, I actually had to cut the number of ability points back to mundane mortal levels.<br /> <br /> (I think at least one of the old players guides presents the idea of secondary skills costing 3 freebie points for 2 dots instead of the usual 2 for 1.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-13-2019, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T05:49:11-08:00","id":1350003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1340739#post1340739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Magick rules have gone back to 2nd / Sorceror's Crusade by default; The total amount of Arete successes counts for all the effect's properties (Only when using Damage + Duration at once does one of them have to be split out.).</div> </div> </div> </div> Holy crap I totally did not get that! I feel like I've read through the magic rules a few times already and never picked up on this! Would you so kind as to tell me which page(s) of the book in particular explain this? I really thought it was still Revised style!!! (though this explains why I was so bewildered by the inclusion of the text box discussing optionally splitting successes among different aspects of the effect...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T07:48:08-08:00","id":1350014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1340676-m20-v-mrev?p=1350003#post1350003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Holy crap I totally did not get that! I feel like I've read through the magic rules a few times already and never picked up on this! Would you so kind as to tell me which page(s) of the book in particular explain this? I really thought it was still Revised style!!! (though this explains why I was so bewildered by the inclusion of the text box discussing optionally splitting successes among different aspects of the effect...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, the Revised style *is* the Optional Divided Successes rule.<br /> <br /> Else, Page 543 onward explains the cases when using or not using that rule.<br /> * Damage AND Duration combined always need split dice - you have choose which one of the two properties you want to do extra separate succesesses for.<br /> * Targets, unless you use the Revised rule, are one target per base success. The rules keep it vague what 'spells can affect several targets'. ST decision I guess.<br /> * Range is usually line of sight/other sensory perceptions. Targets at the fringe of your sensory perceptions increase the Arete diff by +1 (Obscured by fog, just shadows etc.), but if you have Correspondence 3+ then that difficulty is gone - You just need to reach the according total successes matching the correspondence chart - no extra additional dice needed. Again, included in the overall succeses.<br /> <br /> So, without the Revised rule, the only succeses separate from all that are those you either spend in damage or duration, if you want to make use of both at once.<br /> <br /> And there you go <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-21-2019, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}